{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02VV", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fully-faithful}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d84c9fd412ff5e5a625ed5de3738cf6322ea68d872cd73c4a79903e45fb04bb0", "source_text": "Fully faithfulness of the pullback functors", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aae65b5c44d87b2169845af854d4dd77606e05dcd9efbdfeff890b376ed2e326", "unit_id": "tag:02VV:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02VV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fpqc-universal-effective-epimorphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a433f44ee91eaaaec61564aa3f70ae8e96e42840cb21558b20675f6a620649c0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt turns out that the pullback functor between descent data\nfor fpqc-coverings is fully faithful. In other words, morphisms of schemes\nsatisfy fpqc descent. The goal of this section\nis to prove this. The reader is encouraged instead to prove this him/herself.\nThe key is to use Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:194ed9003f2493cb9634ff964018f78888d841f8a886456cf09f72fd554d76b5", "unit_id": "tag:02VV:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02VV", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-surjective-flat-epi}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8e563fcee2db722b9bb34315817d382b0ba116cd7f41645d42c82a22400d1e5b", "source_text": "A surjective and flat morphism is an epimorphism in the\ncategory of schemes.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:15a65d3070c10bf033365bf1b9628cae409c8f92b3b142534ff44e6fb49e6dd2", "unit_id": "tag:02VW:statement"}
